        <div class="row pb-7">
          <div class="col-12">
            <h3 class="text-right mb-7">Improve the online brand presence, experience and integrity.</h3>
          </div>
          <div class="col-lg-8 col-12">
            <p>Without question, luxury and performance will always be synonymous with the Porsche brand. However, we find ourselves at an inflection point for all luxury brands. The internet and the pandemic have permanently altered the landscape. The internet has democratized luxury brands, while the pandemic has heightened customer scrutiny.</p>
            <p>To establish brand preference in the post-pandemic era, brands must adopt a more humanistic approach and showcase how they can enrich lives and bring more meaning to their customers’ experiences.</p>
            <p>How does Porsche enhance lives and preserve the heritage of the brand? By building upon the luxury and performance associations while infusing a more personal touch – emphasizing the owners’ experiences before focusing on the product. Creating an emotional connection that resonates with potential customers, speaking truthfully about the products in simple terms. Both the digital experience and showrooms should reflect this humanistic approach.</p>
            <p class="text-xl">Porsche: Love to Drive</p>
            <p>This positioning isn’t revolutionary; rather, it’s evolutionary. “Love to Drive” can carry the same aspirational halo effect that all desirable brands share. Even those that might not perfectly fit under the Love to Drive theme still aspire to be associated with it.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="row pb-6">
          <div class="col d-flex justify-content-end">
            <img style="width: 400px; max-width: 100%;" src="./assets/porsche-drive-1.jpg" loading="lazy">
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="row pb-6">
          <div class="col-12">
            <h3 class="mb-7">How do we reach our destination from here?</h3>
          </div>
          <div class="col-lg-8 offset-lg-4 col-12">
            <p>The most successful luxury automobile brands have read the tea leaves and have been busy building more humanistic brands for years – some better at executing than others in a most challenging and competitive landscape. The good news is that Porsche is one of this market’s most respected and recognizable brands. Some say Porsche ‘owns’ the luxury performance market. At any rate, now is the perfect time to evolve and put more distance between you and the competition.</p>
            <p>Two questions you can use as a rudder to guide you toward your ideal brand identity are:</p>
            <p>Is it personal? And Is it personalized?</p>
            <p>Use these to measure the success or failure of any activity, feature, product, or branded experience.</p>
            <p>Making it personal assures you are speaking to your customers in terms that are important to them.</p>
            <p>Making it personalized ensures you are creating with your customers in mind. Porsche has an opportunity to define the standards of personalization for the market.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="row pb-6">
          <div class="col-12">
            <img style="max-width: 100%;" src="./assets/porsche-drive-2.jpg" loading="lazy">
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="row pb-6">
          <div class="col-12">
            <h3 class="text-right mb-7">Improve digital capability, efficiency and flexibility.</h3>
          </div>
          <div class="col-lg-8 col-12">
            <h4 class="text-base font-weight-bold mb-0">Porsche’s Composable Commerce Architecture - Driving Digital Excellence almost as fast as your vehicles.</h4>
            <p>We understand your challenge. You boast the most reputable performance cars on the market, yet your legacy monolithic Commerce, CMS, and Marketing system can feel as outdated.</p>
            <p>With over 20 years of eCommerce experience, Royal Cyber has test-driven and implemented various eCommerce systems. That’s why we recommend a composable commerce platform that’s akin to driving a Porsche in many ways. Your team should feel exhilarated as they create personalized experiences at lightning speed that resonate with your fans. Empowering them to make new feature and technology selections will allow your brand to evolve with market demands and even revolutionize customer experiences, putting you ahead of the luxury vehicle brand pack.
            <p>Royal Cyber suggests a modern, composable commerce platform, with key components already in use at Porsche Germany and Porsche US Lifestyle eCommerce platform benchmark sites. What better proof than considering Porsche’s own sites as benchmarks for the new PCA Lifestyle eCommerce platform! Based on our expert assessment, the MACH aligned vendor capabilities, such as Commercetools commerce platform; Contentful content management; Algolia Search & Merchandising; which form the core of the Porsche AG composable Commerce platform, will meet PCA’s objectives as outlined in this RFP.</p>
            <p>The best part is that you don’t have to reinvent the wheel. By leveraging and localizing the ecosystem of an eCommerce platform already preconfigured with Commercetools, Algolia, Contentful, ERP, Headless storefront, Progressive Web Apps (PWA), and cloud services, Porsche can embrace a dynamic and future-proof digital commerce strategy.</p>
            <p>So, why choose Royal Cyber? We are as enthusiastic about Porsche as you are. Our company’s core strength lies in implementing eCommerce and Digital Customer Experience (CX) solutions with exceptional results. Royal Cyber has been instrumental in numerous projects that delivered transformative digital shopping experiences, backed by customer testimonials to prove it. Moreover, what sets us apart is our commitment to bringing our own innovations to each engagement, including 3D visualizers, AI, Neural Search & Product Recommendation capabilities, technical platform accelerators to fast-track time to value – and much more!</p>
            <h4 class="text-base font-weight-bold mb-0">You’re in the Driving Seat:</h4>
            <p>Porsche Germany’s and Porsche US’s adoption of a composable commerce architecture for Lifestyle eCommerce has revolutionized its online presence, allowing the brand to maintain a cutting-edge position in the digital commerce landscape. With the flexibility to leverage best-of-breed components and the power of cloud-native technologies, these teams deliver exceptional customer experiences.</p>
            <p>These platforms offer composability in more ways than just adding new components; they can also be componentized or regionalized for local use. Royal Cyber is proposing two options that we can configure for PCA to ensure you’re in the driving seat:
              <ol>
                <li>Replicate the Porsche Germany and Porsche US Lifestyle eCommerce platform using the same composable software modules – including configurations, templates, content, etc. In other words, ‘copy and paste’ the platform to expedite your own deployment.</li>
                <li>Leverage the Porsche Germany and Porsche US Lifestyle eCommerce platform, with localized components, spaces, or configurations tailored to PCA’s requirements. This option would be more economical and can be quickly configured and deployed for PCA use.</li>
              </ol>
            </p>
            <p>We’re convinced that your team would ‘Love to Drive’ this new platform, just as Porsche enthusiasts love to drive your cars!</p>
            <h4 class="text-base font-weight-bold mb-0">Improving Brand Presence and Customer Experience:</h4>
            <p>With this composable Commerce platform, Porsche can swiftly adapt to emerging trends and customer preferences by adopting a composable commerce approach. The headless storefront allows seamless integration with the latest front-end technologies, creating visually stunning and personalized customer journeys. This flexibility empowers Porsche to maintain a strong brand presence while delivering tailored customer experiences across all touchpoints.</p>
            <h4 class="text-base font-weight-bold mb-0">Ensuring Data Integrity and Digital Capability:</h4>
            <p>By integrating Contentful and ERP systems, Porsche’s composable commerce architecture provides data integrity and accuracy across all channels. The Contentful platform facilitates centralized content management, enabling consistent messaging and brand storytelling. Simultaneously, ERP integration streamlines inventory management and order processing, resulting in a smooth and efficient digital capability that keeps Porsche at the forefront of digital commerce operations.</p>
            <h4 class="text-base font-weight-bold mb-0">Efficiency and Scalability through Cloud Adoption:</h4>
            <p>By harnessing the power of cloud services, Porsche achieves unparalleled efficiency and scalability. Cloud-based architecture enables elastic resources, auto-scaling, and a pay-as-you-go model, optimizing cost-effectiveness while seamlessly handling traffic peaks and growth demands, thus empowering Porsche to deliver flawless performance to customers, regardless of the traffic volume.</p>
            <h4 class="text-base font-weight-bold mb-0">Unleashing Potential with Progressive Web Apps (PWA):</h4>
            <p>Porsche’s embrace of Progressive Web Apps (PWA) significantly enhances the user experience on various devices, irrespective of internet connectivity. PWAs deliver fast loading times, smooth interactions, and app-like experiences, leading to higher customer engagement, improved conversion rates, and increased customer loyalty.</p>
            <h4 class="text-base font-weight-bold mb-0">Creating Unique Shopping Experiences with Algolia:</h4>
            <p>The integration of Algolia, a powerful search and discovery platform, enriches Porsche’s online shopping experience. Customers can effortlessly find products, services, and relevant content, thanks to Algolia’s lightning-fast search capabilities. A search experience like this enhances user satisfaction and increases the likelihood of converting visitors into loyal Porsche enthusiasts.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="row pb-6">
          <div class="col-12">
            <h3 class="mb-7">Improve usability for all user segments.</h3>
          </div>
          <div class="col-lg-8 offset-lg-4 col-12">
            <p>The Platform Transformation requirements are comprehensive, and following your list will provide an exceptional user experience. That said, various ways exist to execute a design and still comply with the requirements. When styling a design to support the brand associations of Porsche, elegance, cleanliness, and sophistication are expected. These are the qualities we would concentrate on in our UI. From pages to components, we seek the same attention to detail you would expect from Porsche.</p>
            <p>In addition to the features listed, we have identified other areas that should be included or considered.</p>
            <h4 class="text-base font-weight-bold mb-0">Mobile First. Why?</h4>
            <ul>
              <li>Improved User Experience: After an exhilarating drive, the Porsche driver steps out into the chill air and decides they need a jacket – remembering an email from the Porsche Lifestyle team, they can go onto the mobile-first site and browses the latest offers related to jackets, then with a few clicks, purchase the jacket for the excursion. According to Statista, mobile devices accounted for 53.3% of all global web traffic in 2022. With mobile use increasing, adopting a mobile-first approach is a critical commerce strategy.</li>
              <li>Better SEO: Google and other search engines favor mobile-friendly websites, so a mobile-first approach can help your website rank higher in search results.</li>
              <li>Reduced Development Costs: Developing a mobile-first website is more cost-effective than developing separate desktop and mobile websites/apps.</li>
            </ul>
            <h4 class="text-base font-weight-bold mb-0">Effective Navigation and User Controls. Why?</h4>
            <ul>
              <li>A Seamless Web Experience: Users will get personalized quick navigation, based on their user profile and other indicating details, tailored to their needs – for instance, finding that jacket quickly.</li>
              <li>Orientation: Users will clearly understand where they are on the website, how they got there, and how to navigate to other desired sections.</li>
              <li>Intuitiveness: Users will intuitively understand how to move back and forth from a given page.</li>
              <li>Accessible Navigation: We must ensure that users can view and understand the navigation in any context, avoiding mixing navigation with background images and other graphics.</li>
            </ul>
            <h4 class="text-base font-weight-bold mb-0">Optimized Graphics. Why?</h4>
            <ul>
              <li>Improved User Experience: Optimized images help products retain almost the original quality while being smaller in size, improving site performance.</li>
              <li>Faster Loading Times: Optimized images load faster, especially important on mobile devices where data speeds can be slower.</li>
              <li>SEO Benefits: Search engines like Google can index images, so optimizing them can help your website rank higher in search results, driving more traffic and potentially more sales.</li>
              <li>Bandwidth Savings: Optimized images take up less space on your website’s server, saving you money on bandwidth costs and • ensuring scalability as your web content grows.</li>
            </ul>
            <h4 class="text-base font-weight-bold mb-0">Usability Testing. Why?</h4>
            <ul>
              <li>Identifying Usability Issues: Usability testing helps identify issues on the website that may not have been apparent. These issues can range from minor annoyances to major usability problems that hinder users from completing their goals.</li>
              <li>Design Feedback: User testing provides valuable feedback on the overall look, feel, and functionality of your website, helping to improve the user experience.</li>
              <li>Design Feedback: User testing provides valuable feedback on the overall look, feel, and functionality of your website, helping to improve the user experience.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
