            <h3 class="mb-7">Improve data and analytics insights to support conversion metrics.</h3>
          </div>
          <div class="col-lg-8 offset-lg-4 col-12">
            <p>Yes, the absence of tracking makes it impossible to pinpoint where you are today and determine your path to success. But this can be an opportunity for improvement. We can help you build a site from scratch that continually measures its ongoing health. And just as importantly, we can teach you how to constantly take your customers’ pulse to ensure you always provide for their changing needs.</p>
            <h4 class="text-base font-weight-bold mb-0">How do we do it?</h4>
            <p>With the right tools and a focus on customer behavior. We will thoroughly assess your current needs and consider how fast and big your customer base will grow. Based on this information, we will advise you on the right suite of tools that fit your needs - Adobe Analytics if you want to be aggressive and Google GA4 if your projections are modest.</p>
            <p>In the area of Customer Experience Analytics (CXA), there are two tools we would like you to consider: Acoustic Tealeaf and Lucky Orange. Both are excellent for monitoring customer behavior, but each has its inherent strengths. Tealeaf is particularly adept at determining the root causes of customer issues, while Lucky Orange excels at analyzing web applications.</p>
            <p>Of course, data collection is one thing; figuring out what it means is another. With our dedicated CXA team, we can help you monitor customer behavior, identify friction points, and test solutions.</p>
            <p>Data analytics are incredibly valuable to your business, helping you understand what’s working and what isn’t in your ads, as well as how people are using your website and the products they buy the most. Data analytics allow you to determine your customers’ wants and needs and improve your product offerings to better suit their requirements. Here are the ways to improve conversion:</p>
          </div>
        </div>
