            <h2>3. A New Brand Identity for a Trusted Icon.</h2>
            <span style="font-size: 6rem;" class="font-weight-bold mb-3">Sorel</span>
            <p>Pac boots for the dead of winter – that’s a long way from the runway. Such was the challenge for evolving a brand that saved feet from freezing to a year-round fashion statement. Never losing sight that functionally was the key – fashion fused with functionality was the unique brand association and my team, and I set out to own it.</p>
            <p>A new brand voice was born. One that captured a fashion-forward attitude but with an undercurrent of toughness – not brute strength, more like resolve. “Thanks, Sorel, I can trudge through all the crap a Wisconsin winter can muster and still look great” – typical feelings of a brand evangelist. Reviews like this mean consumers are getting the duality messaging.</p>
            <p>The new Kinetic line was the brand yelling, “we got a whole new level of fashion and functionality here.” The “Sorel DNA” was still there; a rugged outsole and exaggerated proportions, but the sneaker market was not felt liners and sealed seams. We needed to drive home “duality” but differently. Messaging that suggested multi-purpose and contrast – a solution that made the positioning more pliable.</p>
          </div>
